  "summary_md": "**Michael Kirchhof ([@mkirchhof_](https://x.com/mkirchhof_/status/2115452992220762302))** and Apple ML Research colleagues generated **458,752 RL environments** (64 apps, 10,472 APIs) to train an agent on stateful, multi-step on-device tasks. The 9-part self-thread explains the three-phase Gemini-built env pipeline, says their Qwen 3.5 27B finetune ranks near the top of AppWorld, and shows that data-composition scaling laws predict when to add diversity rather than more prompts.",
  "referenced_urls": [
    {
      "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.37648",
      "short_url": "https://t.co/lqyzIyvvtF",
      "title": "Scaling Laws for Tool-Use Agents via Controllable Environment Synthesis",
      "from_post": "2115452992220762302"
    }
  ],
  "hashtags": [],
  "topics": [
    "local-models",
    "agentic-cognition"
  ],
  "relevance": "Scaling laws for synthetic tool-use environments, with a ~30B open model as the trained agent.",
